              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "coriārius, coriāriī — \"a tanner, a currier\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Coriārius coria bovum in aquā lavat. The tanner washes the hides of the oxen in water."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Second declension, masculine: coriārius, coriāriī m., from corium 'hide, leather'. Tanneries stank and stood at the edge of town. English currier comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "coriārius is built on corium 'hide, leather' with the suffix -ārius (Lewis & Short). English currier, a leather dresser, comes from it through French."
            }
          ]
        },
